# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded log-gamma function of B64
#
# log|gamma(x)| in double-double with an error bound: -log|x| plus a series for
# |x| < 0.5, piece-wise polynomials on [0.5, 8.29541] (with the zeros at 1 and
# 2 factored out), Stirling's series above, and the reflection formula for
# negative x. When the bound can't decide the rounding, an accurate phase redoes
# it in triple-double, with polynomials around the zeros of lgamma between
# -10.5 and -2, and a table settles the hardest inputs. Only the value is
# computed: C's signgam (the sign of gamma(x)) is not. Round to nearest only:
# 0, the negative integers and +-inf give +inf, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# The double-double helpers and the fast logarithm come from Tgamma.te.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/lgamma/lgamma.c via RazorForge's B64Lgamma.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2024 Alexei Sibidanov <sibid@uvic.ca>
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module System/Numerics/B64

